// The service directory's interface (ADR-0005 C12, ADR-0011 N9): the way a program reaches the
// services its launcher gave it.
//
// Its types, server and client are generated into sdk/directory (`cargo xtask regenerate`, with
// `oidl generate --library origin.directory`). `cargo xtask check` fails if that code is not what
// this file generates, or if this file's ABI is not the one origin.directory.lock records. The
// directory's logic is services/directory. How a launcher fills a directory, and how a provider
// receives the connections a directory passes it, are not decided yet (step 4): they are not here.

/// The service directory (ADR-0005 C12, ADR-0011 N9). A program finds services only through the
/// channel its start record names DIRECTORY, and the process its launcher chose serves this
/// interface on it. What the directory holds is the launcher's choice.
library origin.directory;
transport channel;
version 0.1;
use origin.kernel;

/// A program's service directory.
interface directory {
    /// Passes server, the server end of a channel the caller made, to the provider of the
    /// interface interface_id at major major: the identity a hello names (docs/spec/OIDL.md
    /// §7.7). The caller may use the other end at once, before this replies: the kernel holds
    /// what it writes until the provider reads it. Success means the end was passed on, not that
    /// the provider has read it. not_found: this directory holds no provider of that interface
    /// and major. limit: the provider cannot take the end now. On either error the end is closed,
    /// so the caller's end reports peer_closed.
    method connect = 1 (
        /// The interface, as its hello names it.
        interface_id: u64,
        /// Its major version.
        major: u16,
        /// The end the provider serves: it reads, writes and waits on it, and the directory
        /// passes it on.
        server: handle<channel, read | write | wait | transfer>,
    ) errors(not_found, limit) requires none;
}
